121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 102 0 R
/T (global traffic volumes rising sharply year over year. This growth strains existing infrastructure and creates significant challenges for city planners and traffic management authorities. Traditional traffic monitoring methods4including inductive loops embedded in  roadways and manual counting procedures4are not only expensive to install and  maintain but also highly disruptive to traffic flow during implementation. These legacy  systems lack the flexibility and scalability needed for modern smart city initiatives. There's an urgent need for scalable, real-time, and accurate vehicle counting and  classification solutions that can adapt to dynamic traffic conditions without requiring  extensive physical infrastructure changes.)
/E (global traffic volumes rising sharply year over year. This growth strains existing infrastructure and creates significant challenges for city planners and traffic management authorities. Traditional traffic monitoring methods4including inductive loops embedded in  roadways and manual counting procedures4are not only expensive to install and  maintain but also highly disruptive to traffic flow during implementation. These legacy  systems lack the flexibility and scalability needed for modern smart city initiatives. There's an urgent need for scalable, real-time, and accurate vehicle counting and  classification solutions that can adapt to dynamic traffic conditions without requiring  extensive physical infrastructure changes.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
